<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11152"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 10:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I started thinking about this before the arrest, &#40;everything done in multiples of 3&#41;but now I am incorporating the theory of 3 into perps also. <BR> <BR>What if they all &#40; I believe 3 of them&#41; participated in the Otero crime in 74. Then they went their separate ways, but they would get together to plan the next one, and each guy would have to do the same victim type and mo, we have <BR>the first case, which is  <BR> <BR>Otero <BR> <BR>Killed 3 Jo Otero&#39;s <BR> <BR>3 bags  <BR> <BR>3 &#34;O&#34;s in each of the 3 Jo&#39;s names        <BR> <BR>3 in addy, 803 North Edgemoor, which also hase 3 &#34;O&#34;s <BR> <BR>Now they separate and commit killings in sets of 3 <BR> <BR>3 cars taken to shopping place <BR> <BR>3 older women, &#40;including Anna&#41; <BR> <BR>3 moms at home with kids <BR> <BR>3 under bridges <BR> <BR>3 Artist sketches that dont match eachother, so there were  3 eyewitnesses, &#40;maybe done on purpose so there would be differing accounts&#41; <BR> <BR>3 poems <BR> <BR>3 stabbings <BR> <BR>3 packages found outside with postcards <BR> <BR>3 puzzle grids <BR> <BR>3 fake ids   &#40;2 ids and one badge&#41; <BR> <BR>things to find out: <BR> <BR>how many drivers licenses taken, I have Fox Wegerle Hedge Davis <BR> <BR>how many broken windows, I have Fox Davis, Anna and Bright   <BR> <BR>how many phones cuts, I have Hedge Otero Casey Williams and Davis <BR> <BR>how many drownings, or found in tubs  <BR> <BR>how many shootings,  <BR> <BR>how many blunt force trauma to head <BR> <BR>how many stabbed and dumped, I have Olsen and Albright <BR> <BR>how many fires, I have Mould and Smith <BR> <BR>I think they will all be multiples of 3 <BR> <BR>I think we should study more about the Fa   ger case, that would have been the second family. Btk the writer, wrote to say that he didnt commit the crime, my opinion is that he left out the fact that one of his partners did it.  Maybe butterworth was one of the three,  and the rule for this crime was, you had to kill one of your partners neighbors. <BR> <BR>Please help fill in the missing info, <BR>or you call me completely crazy. Id really to hear what others think.  <BR>  <BR>and about the 3 dudes letter, btk the writer wrote it becuse he knew he was going to to be seeing the police soon, hence, the cops would then have 3 guys. guess he mailed it too early, or the cops were slow in picking him up.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
