<!--Post: 11577--><!--Time: 1110917618-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11577"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Zenith<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Zenith<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 12:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m really curious about the 3 thing. Is there a psychological name for it? Does it exist as a specific condition? <BR> <BR>We suffered some serious harrassment at home, apparently from a person who hates us that we moved in two houses from without realizing. We noticed a clear pattern of 3s in all the stuff that happened, and it made it really hard to catch them because about the time you realized something was really being done to you, they moved on to something else. <BR> <BR>So I&#39;m just curious if this 3 thing is really some sort of a psychological condition that can exist, I saw a fictional cop show on tv about it and it made me wonder if it was real. Anyone know?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11577-->
<!--Post: 11596--><!--Time: 1110932105-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11596"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 4:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am very skeptical about how people percieve three&#39;s. People tend to see things that can be easily comprehended and three is a perfect example. It is three. It has a begining, a middle and an end. It provides and easy clear way to grasp things on a simple plane than be overburdened with too much information. That&#39;s why in many jokes there are three charecters, or three situations or three choices. In game shows three doors, behind one sits the coveted prize. In explaining something there are often three examples of reference. In baseball three strikes and you&#39;re out. In selling something there are three procuct examples. It just sounds better, it has a flow. <BR>People think of famous people dying in three&#39;s which is not true at all. Famous people die almost every day. Someone will single out a famous actor, a famous blues muscian and another famous actor who have died within a few days and say they always die in threes. In the meantime an actor even more famous than the two has died but he was from another earlier era and to the person who has noticed the three deaths they had never heard of that actor. Also in the meantime the world&#39;s most famous jazz muscian has died but they are into blues and never heard of the jazz guy so they didn&#39;t notice he died. Also in the meantime the world&#39;s most renouned Nobel winning physicist has died but they had never heard of them and a best selling author who won a Pulitzer prize and won an Oscar for a screenplay has died but they didn&#39;t take note of it. So in seven days, seven very famous people died but they had only heard of three of them so they think death comes in threes. <BR>I am a three. I was born on the third day of the third month, the third child born to a thrity three year old mother. Heck, i could even add on the third floor of a three sylable named hospital in a state with three sylables and on and on. The number three plays no more significant role in my life than any other number.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11596-->
<!--Post: 11646--><!--Time: 1110980001-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11646"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 5:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Zenith: it could be that it takes at least 2 to 3 instances before you realize that there is a pattern developing. Then one is on their guard and anticipating the next event. Too much repetition will get one caught, i.e., BTK drops. Perhaps that is why the pattern changed. Harrassment is terrible. I lived in a subdivision where the children were spawned by who knows what. I actually purchased an anti-terrorism handbook to try to get insight into what was happening and how to deal with it.  People who harrass are inbred jackasses, to be sure. You have my empathy. <BR> <BR>Itty, it has been my experience as well that it seems to be a consistent event. One movie star dies and 2 more will follow. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11646-->
<!--Post: 11652--><!--Time: 1111003317-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11652"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Zenith<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Zenith<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 12:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Agreed that most of the &#34;3&#34; stuff is just superstition of sorts. But I&#39;m still curious with whether there is an actual psychological disorder having to do with 3s. Maybe an obsessive compulsive disorder. But I&#39;m only speculating and want to know if it&#39;s factual.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11652-->
<!--Post: 11676--><!--Time: 1111020727-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11676"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 4:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->One is an instance, two is a coincidence, three is a pattern.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11676-->
<!--Post: 11696--><!--Time: 1111033023-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11696"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 8:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Three parts of the person me, myself and I <BR>In Rader&#39;s case, Husband Father, and Serial Killer<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11696-->
<!--Post: 11852--><!--Time: 1111279930-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11852"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 4:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Not to make lite of this subject but there was a book published 30 yrs ago by pro football player Gail Sayers titled &#34;I am 3rd&#34; His motto in life was &#34;God is first, my family second, and I am 3rd.&#34;  <BR> <BR>Is it possible that Rader was in anyway a sports fan more specifically football and might have read this book ?  The majority of the book deals with this philosophy where he is 3rd on the list of his life priorities and he needed to be three different men to become the best man.  .  .  it&#39;s a stretch.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11852-->
<!--Post: 11870--><!--Time: 1111307569-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11870"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 20, 2005 - 12:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is another example of three, remember Dennis Rader is Lutheran and Lutherans like Catholics share in the teaching of God in Trinity of the Athanasian Creed. Father, Son and Holy spirit.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11870-->
<!--Post: 11878--><!--Time: 1111334291-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11878"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 20, 2005 - 7:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe he played baseball: three strikes and you&#39;re out. Perhaps he took the sighting of a person 3 times as a &#39;sign&#39; that they were the chosen one. How many times does three show up in the general addresses in Wichita? We cannot figure out how his perverted little mind thinks. He definitely does not use the same logic as most people. <BR> <BR>If you put a straight line in front of the three, you have a B. Turn it on its side and you have part of his symbol. Add dots and you have nipples and breasts. Could he have dabbled in the study of witchcraft and bought the theory that the devil&#39;s children are fed by a third breast under the witch&#39;s arm? GAG!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11878-->
